    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our highest-projected asset at 68.82, leveraging a massive +19% SP Skill boost against the vulnerable Paredes. He is joined by the reliable table-setters **Luis Arraez** (64.64) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.50), both of whom capitalize on a soft matchup against Gusto. The Gusto start is a focal point for our strategy; his slow delivery profile has elevated the projections for **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Luis Arraez**, granting them a +2% SB efficiency bump\u2014a critical edge in our focus on stealing bases. While **Tyler Freeman** sits at 62.19, his value is uniquely driven by a +14% park factor, making him a high-floor start despite a moderate SP matchup.\n\nConversely, we are exercising extreme caution with our middle infield and platoon spots. **Bryson Stott** (42.54) and **Jonathan Aranda** (42.64) hover just above the benching threshold; **Bryson Stott** is particularly handicapped by a negative platoon split and the presence of an elite catcher, though he remains in the lineup due to his potential contribution to our 5x5 totals. **Jeremiah Jackson** was the final player left on the cutting room floor with a 38.07, narrowly missing the cut because his bottom-of-the-order positioning (-8%) outweighed his marginal platoon advantage. We are monitoring **Taylor Ward** closely; despite his leadoff spot, his 44.15 score is heavily pressured by a -16% SP skill penalty against Sheehan, marking him as a high-risk play today. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** still sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, and we will need **Cal Raleigh** to maintain his 61.41 efficiency to anchor the bottom of the order against Tolle.",
